    "probe_text": "Verified against the actual YAML and function classes. Here is the complete ordered chain for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## What actually handles it\n\nThere is no `@RestController` \u2014 the endpoint is the OfficeFloor pipeline in `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`, a linear chain of function classes. The OfficeFloor starter (`officefloor-rest-spring-boot-4-starter`, v4.0.2) is present in `pom.xml`, so this is live. Steps run in the exact `next:` order below.\n\n## Validations and side-effects, in order\n\n**0. Authorization** *(YAML `composition.authorize`, line 2)* \u2014 `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` (i.e. `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`), enforced via `@EnableMethodSecurity`, active only when `petclinic.security.enable=true`. Failure \u2192 `AuthorizationDeniedException` handler.\n\n**0b. Bean validation on the body** \u2014 the request binds to the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerFieldsDto`, which carries JSR-380 constraints (`@NotNull`/`@Pattern`/`@Size` on firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone; `@Email`+`@Size` on email; `@Pattern ^[0-9]{4}$` on postcode). If OfficeFloor triggers `@RequestBody` validation these fire first as `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 400. Note the DTO's `sharesHousehold` field is documented as overriding the household rule but **no pipeline step ever reads it** \u2014 it is dead.\n\nThen the pipeline (`validate` step runs **outside** the transaction; every step from `ensureUniqueIdentity` onward is governed by one shared `transaction`):\n\n**1. `ValidateOwnerFields`** \u2014 in this order:\n   - Normalizes `address` (`OwnerAddress.normalize`: trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST\u2192STREET / RD\u2192ROAD / AVE\u2192AVENUE) and writes it back.\n   - Requires non-blank `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (after normalize), `city`, `telephone`; any blank/whitespace-only \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400, listing the missing fields).\n   - Normalizes `telephone` to E.164 (`OwnerTelephone.toE164`) and writes it back; unparseable \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400).\n   - Normalizes `email` (blank\u2192null, else must match syntax, lower-cased) and writes it back; present-but-invalid \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` (400).\n   - Normalizes `postcode` (blank\u2192null, else 4 digits and within the city's regional range) and writes it back; invalid \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n   - Republishes the mutated DTO for later steps.\n\n**2. `EnsureIdentityUnique`** \u2014 scans all owners (`findAll`); if the new owner's identity key (canonical telephone | email | householdId) exactly matches an existing owner \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**).\n\n**3. `EnsureCityCapacity`** \u2014 counts existing owners in the same city (trim/case-insensitive); if \u2265 50 \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (**409**).\n\n**4. `EnsureDailyOwnerLimit`** \u2014 rolls the effective registration date forward off weekends to a business day, counts existing owners on that day; if \u2265 100 \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (**429**).\n\n*(From here, side-effects only \u2014 no more rejections.)*\n\n**5. `BuildOwner`** \u2014 maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity (ignoring id/pets) and sets its `registrationDate` to the rolled-forward business day.\n\n**6. `AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where NNNN is (count of owners in that city)+1, zero-padded.\n\n**7. `AssignHouseholdId`** \u2014 finds household peers (same normalized lastName + address); sets `householdSize` = peers+1; if peers exist, derives a deterministic `householdId` and **back-fills + saves** that id onto any peers that lacked one (extra write side-effects to other rows).\n\n**8. `CountNamesakes`** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners with the same first+last name.\n\n**9. `FlagBulkSignup`** \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` if more than 80 owners already exist on that business day.\n\n**10. `SaveOwner`** \u2014 `ownerRepository.save(owner)` (the primary insert).\n\n**11. `AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 logs the creation to the `AUDIT` logger (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel).\n\n**12. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto` (deriving displayName, initials, locality, membershipNumber, membershipLevel, contactPreference, identityKey) and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nThe whole thing (steps 2\u201312) commits as a single governed transaction at the end; only step 1's validation runs before the transaction opens."
